SI-3 stage 5 (SI3-5): the SI-1 and SI-2 censuses archived as pinned artifacts

SI1-5 and SI2-4, the live census re-measurements whose old side was the
legacy machinery, are replaced -- not silently deleted -- by
artifact-integrity checks: each census.json is pinned by the blob
identity it has carried since its round landed (SI-1 at 7a3e6288, SI-2
at d6b2e505) with a one-byte drift control, and labelled in the guard a
certified historical measurement of its round's checkpoint under its
round's rule, never read as evidence about the current head, with no
old/new equivalence claimed after retirement. The four harness
functions that ran the retired side (_si1_census, _si1_control_census,
_si2_census, _si2_control_census) are deleted with the clauses that
called them; every U3-side measurement keeps running, and the scoped
record set still feeds SI2-8.

